<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>The Monomial can be Recovered in Polynomial Time</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, a solver can form residual labels</p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(k)}\;:=\;y^{(k)}\oplus\bigoplus_{j=1}^{g}a^{(k)}_{j}M_{j}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)\;=\;M_{g+1}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">⊕</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>g</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(k)}\;:=\;y^{(k)}\oplus\bigoplus_{j=1}^{g}a^{(k)}_{j}M_{j}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)\;=\;M_{g+1}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so recovery reduces to identifying the unknown degree-<math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d-1)</annotation></semantics></math> support <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> from labeled payloads.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{+}:=\{k:r^{(k)}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{+}:=\{k:r^{(k)}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T:=|K_{+}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T:=|K_{+}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the decoder</p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{S}\;:=\;\bigcap_{k\in K_{+}}\mathrm{supp}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.877em;" width="1.877em"><mi>supp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{S}\;:=\;\bigcap_{k\in K_{+}}\mathrm{supp}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which outputs <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{S}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{S}|=d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{S}|=d-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and otherwise declares failure.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Poly-time recovery under fixed-weight payloads)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix an instance and assume payloads are i.i.d. uniform on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v\in\{0,1\}^{p}:\|v\|_{0}=w^{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v\in\{0,1\}^{p}:\|v\|_{0}=w^{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}\geq d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}\geq d-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho=\rho(w^{\star})=\Pr[M_{g+1}(v)=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\rho(w^{\star})=\Pr[M_{g+1}(v)=1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=|K_{+}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=|K_{+}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[T=0]=(1-\rho)^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[T=0]=(1-\rho)^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, conditioned on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the decoder succeeds with probability at least</span></p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\min\Big\{1,\;(p-(d-1))\Big(\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}\Big)^{T}\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\min\Big\{1,\;(p-(d-1))\Big(\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}\Big)^{T}\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(k)}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(k)}=1</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{g+1}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{g+1}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which is equivalent to
<math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{g+1}\subseteq\mathrm{supp}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.877em;" width="1.877em"><mi>supp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{g+1}\subseteq\mathrm{supp}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus for every <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in K_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in K_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{g+1}\subseteq\mathrm{supp}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.877em;" width="1.877em"><mi>supp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{g+1}\subseteq\mathrm{supp}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{g+1}\subseteq\bigcap_{k\in K_{+}}\mathrm{supp}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)\;=\;\widehat{S}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">⊆</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.877em;" width="1.877em"><mi>supp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{g+1}\subseteq\bigcap_{k\in K_{+}}\mathrm{supp}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)\;=\;\widehat{S}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, conditioned on <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the intersection decoder can fail only if <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{S}</annotation></semantics></math> contains at least one
<em id="A2.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">extraneous</em> coordinate <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\notin S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\notin S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., some <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[p]\setminus S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[p]\setminus S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> appears in every positive support.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\notin S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\notin S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and consider a single draw <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1</annotation></semantics></math>
(equivalently, <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{g+1}\subseteq\mathrm{supp}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{g+1}\subseteq\mathrm{supp}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>).
Under the fixed-weight model, after forcing ones on <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the remaining <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}-(d-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}-(d-1)</annotation></semantics></math> ones are chosen
uniformly among the <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-(d-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-(d-1)</annotation></semantics></math> coordinates in <math id="A2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[p]\setminus S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[p]\setminus S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[i\in\mathrm{supp}(v)\mid r=1]\;=\;\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[i\in\mathrm{supp}(v)\mid r=1]\;=\;\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now condition on the event <math id="A2.p4.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{T=|K_{+}|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T=|K_{+}|\}</annotation></semantics></math> and on the index set <math id="A2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> itself. Because the original examples are i.i.d.,
the payloads <math id="A2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v^{(k)}\}_{k\in K_{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v^{(k)}\}_{k\in K_{+}}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. draws from the conditional distribution <math id="A2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v\mid r=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v\mid r=1)</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\Big[i\in\mathrm{supp}(v^{(k)})\ \forall k\in K_{+}\,\Big|\,T\Big]\;=\;\Big(\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}\Big)^{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\Big[i\in\mathrm{supp}(v^{(k)})\ \forall k\in K_{+}\,\Big|\,T\Big]\;=\;\Big(\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}\Big)^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking a union bound over the <math id="A2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-(d-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-(d-1)</annotation></semantics></math> possible extr coordinates gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\big[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}\mid T\big]\;\leq\;\big(p-(d-1)\big)\Big(\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}\Big)^{T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\big[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}\mid T\big]\;\leq\;\big(p-(d-1)\big)\Big(\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}\Big)^{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">which implies (<a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Theorem B.1 (Poly-time recovery under fixed-weight payloads). ‣ Appendix B The Monomial can be Recovered in Polynomial Time ‣ Tool Building as a Path to “Superintelligence”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). Finally, since
<math id="A2.p4.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbf{1}\{r^{(k)}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbf{1}\{r^{(k)}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p4.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[r^{(k)}=1]=\rho=\rho(w^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[r^{(k)}=1]=\rho=\rho(w^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A2.p4.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[T=0]=(1-\rho)^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[T=0]=(1-\rho)^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(High-probability recovery with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> samples)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the setting of Thm. <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (Poly-time recovery under fixed-weight payloads). ‣ Appendix B The Monomial can be Recovered in Polynomial Time ‣ Tool Building as a Path to “Superintelligence”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, let
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho:=\rho(w^{\star})=\Pr[M_{g+1}(v)=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho:=\rho(w^{\star})=\Pr[M_{g+1}(v)=1]</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:=\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:=\frac{w^{\star}-(d-1)}{p-(d-1)}\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Fix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}:=\left\lceil\frac{\log\!\big(2(p-(d-1))/\delta\big)}{\log(1/\alpha)}\right\rceil\quad(\text{and if }\alpha=0,\text{ take }T_{0}:=1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> take </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}:=\left\lceil\frac{\log\!\big(2(p-(d-1))/\delta\big)}{\log(1/\alpha)}\right\rceil\quad(\text{and if }\alpha=0,\text{ take }T_{0}:=1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq\frac{1}{\rho}\max\{2T_{0},\;8\log(2/\delta)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ρ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 8</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq\frac{1}{\rho}\max\{2T_{0},\;8\log(2/\delta)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the decoder in (<a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Appendix B The Monomial can be Recovered in Polynomial Time ‣ Tool Building as a Path to “Superintelligence”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>)
outputs <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{S}=S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{S}=S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T=|K_{+}|=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbf{1}\{r^{(k)}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=|K_{+}|=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbf{1}\{r^{(k)}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(k)}=M_{g+1}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(k)}=M_{g+1}\!\big(v^{(k)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> and the payloads are i.i.d.,
we have <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\sim\mathrm{Bin}(K,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\sim\mathrm{Bin}(K,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Thm. <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (Poly-time recovery under fixed-weight payloads). ‣ Appendix B The Monomial can be Recovered in Polynomial Time ‣ Tool Building as a Path to “Superintelligence”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, for any <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}\mid T=t]\;\leq\;\big(p-(d-1)\big)\alpha^{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}\mid T=t]\;\leq\;\big(p-(d-1)\big)\alpha^{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}]\;\leq\;\Pr[T&lt;T_{0}]\;+\;\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}\mid T\geq T_{0}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}]\;\leq\;\Pr[T&lt;T_{0}]\;+\;\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}\mid T\geq T_{0}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the first term, our lower bound on <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\rho/2\geq T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\rho/2\geq T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, so by a multiplicative Chernoff bound,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[T&lt;T_{0}]\;\leq\;\Pr\!\left[T\leq\tfrac{1}{2}K\rho\right]\;\leq\;\exp\!\left(-\tfrac{1}{8}K\rho\right)\;\leq\;\delta/2," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>K</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>K</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[T&lt;T_{0}]\;\leq\;\Pr\!\left[T\leq\tfrac{1}{2}K\rho\right]\;\leq\;\exp\!\left(-\tfrac{1}{8}K\rho\right)\;\leq\;\delta/2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality uses <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\rho\geq 8\log(2/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\rho\geq 8\log(2/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second term, on <math id="A2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}\mid T\geq T_{0}]\;\leq\;\big(p-(d-1)\big)\alpha^{T_{0}}\;\leq\;\delta/2," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}\mid T\geq T_{0}]\;\leq\;\big(p-(d-1)\big)\alpha^{T_{0}}\;\leq\;\delta/2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">by the definition of <math id="A2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (and trivially if <math id="A2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>). Combining the two bounds yields
<math id="A2.p8.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}]\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\widehat{S}\neq S_{g+1}]\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Lem. <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3 (Bayes masking given observed (𝑎,𝑣)). ‣ 4.2 Statistical Obfuscation: Construction and Guarantees ‣ 4 Theory ‣ Tool Building as a Path to “Superintelligence”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> shows a <em id="A2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">per-sample</em> obfuscation property: marginalizing over the unknown prefix supports,
each labeled example provides only exponentially small Bayes advantage about the next-term signal unless one conditions on the revealed
prefix. In the ideal balanced case <math id="A2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(w^{\star})=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(w^{\star})=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, this advantage is <math id="A2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(a)\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(a)\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
While the trivial leakage case <math id="A2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(a)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math> is theoretically possible, its probability <math id="A2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{-g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{-g}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes exponentially rare as depth increases.
Lem. <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (History-only is prior guessing). ‣ 4.2 Statistical Obfuscation: Construction and Guarantees ‣ 4 Theory ‣ Tool Building as a Path to “Superintelligence”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> rules out history-only shortcuts under the instance distribution, since <math id="A2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> remains uniform given the
revealed prefix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, Thm. <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (Poly-time recovery under fixed-weight payloads). ‣ Appendix B The Monomial can be Recovered in Polynomial Time ‣ Tool Building as a Path to “Superintelligence”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> (and Corollary <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary B.2 (High-probability recovery with 𝐾 samples). ‣ Appendix B The Monomial can be Recovered in Polynomial Time ‣ Tool Building as a Path to “Superintelligence”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>) show that a diligent solver can subtract the prefix mask to obtain residual labels <math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(k)}=M_{g+1}(v^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(k)}=M_{g+1}(v^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math> and recover <math id="A2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> in polynomial time from
<math id="A2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=O\!\big(\tfrac{1}{\rho(w^{\star})}\log(p/\delta)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=O\!\big(\tfrac{1}{\rho(w^{\star})}\log(p/\delta)\big)</annotation></semantics></math> samples with failure probability at most <math id="A2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (for fixed <math id="A2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and constant <math id="A2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(w^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(w^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>). Together, these properties justify using <math id="A2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 4.1 Problem formulation ‣ 4 Theory ‣ Tool Building as a Path to “Superintelligence”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) as an operational measure of step success in our benchmark.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Efficient validation. </span> Given the instance specification (in particular <math id="A2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>) and a candidate monomial <math id="A2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the validator parses <math id="A2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, rejects unless it contains exactly one address variable (which must be <math id="A2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>) and exactly <math id="A2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-1</annotation></semantics></math> distinct payload variables, then accepts iff the parsed payload index set <math id="A2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{S}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="A2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.This runs in time <math id="A2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(|\tilde{t}|+d\log d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|\tilde{t}|+d\log d)</annotation></semantics></math> worst-case (or <math id="A2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(|\tilde{t}|+d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|\tilde{t}|+d)</annotation></semantics></math> expected with hashing).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a></cite></p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
